Description: Modern Linux screen-time enforcement daemon, Material Design 3 UI & CLI
 curfewd tracks and limits desktop usage for user accounts on Linux systems
 with a native unprivileged Material Design 3 desktop UI (curfewd-ui),
 verified multi-DE screen locking (Cinnamon, XFCE, MATE, GNOME, KDE),
 X11 fullscreen-game grab release, individual per-app daily limits,
 Polkit-authorized D-Bus API (org.curfewd.Daemon1), atomic JSON policy storage,
 SQLite usage history, modern curfewctl CLI with --json output, and a
 lightweight auto-reconnecting tray companion.
 .
 Modern successor originally forked from Timekpr-nExT (GPL-3.0-or-later).
 .
 Report bugs at: https://github.com/csmende/curfewd/issues
